  "summary": "Lead the Shop walkthrough with existing default structural admission and correct stale capability claims.",
  "why": "Luis approved parallel documentation and conformance work plus consumer-led requirement discovery. RED distinguishes the old Shop entrypoint and five stale capability claims. GREEN uses the existing runner and no caller-authored check outcomes, preserves frozen predecessor evidence, moves the executable query guard to the default run, and distinguishes public compiler/history/Event roles from unchanged Assent limits. No runtime, ontology, dependencies, packaging or release change. Re-entry and Robotics stay isolated on frozen Core and report concrete generic gaps only. Focused gates: 9 runner tests, 23 historical/time/gap controls, 16 capability/docs checks; groups overlap. Combined validation is recorded in the slice report. Broad gate: 1243 passed and two strict HTML failures for one out-of-tree README link. The corrective explicit-download RED is 605a971; affected HTML/autodoc/entry/AST rerun passes four tests without relaxing warnings. This is decomposed validation, not one uninterrupted all-green full suite.",
